{"url": "https://api.openalex.org/works?search=formal+models+of+epistemic+value+of+information+in+sequential+research+decisions+and+optimal+stopping+theory&per-page=4&select=id%2Cdoi%2Ctitle%2Cpublication_year%2Ctype%2Ccited_by_count%2Copen_access%2Cprimary_location%2Cabstract_inverted_index", "scope": "OpenAlex scholarly metadata and reconstructed abstracts where supplied; not full papers", "excerpt": "[{"id": "https://openalex.org/W7128917653", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.62311/nesx/rb-978-81-997569-7-7", "title": "Quantum Risk Forecasting Under Uncertainty: Bayesian Optimal-Stopping Theorems and Algorithms", "publication_year": 2025, "type": "reference-entry", "cited_by_count": 0, "open_access": {"is_oa": true, "oa_status": "gold", "oa_url": "https://www.nationaleducationservices.org/file-download/1583652/Download Full-Text Research Book PDF Pp1-48J1.pdf", "any_repository_has_fulltext": null}, "primary_location": {"id": "doi:10.62311/nesx/rb-978-81-997569-7-7", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.62311/nesx/rb-978-81-997569-7-7", "is_oa": true, "landing_page_url": "https://doi.org/10.62311/nesx/rb-978-81-997569-7-7", "pdf_url": "https://www.nationaleducationservices.org/file-download/1583652/Download Full-Text Research Book PDF Pp1-48J1.pdf", "source": null, "license": null, "license_id": null, "version": "publishedVersion", "is_accepted": true, "is_published": true, "raw_source_name": null, "raw_type": "reference-book"}, "abstract": "Abstract: Quantum risk forecasting increasingly depends on decisions made under deep uncertainty: unknown data-generating mechanisms, regime shifts, and constraints that make classical asymptotics fragile. This manuscript develops a coherent framework that combines Bayesian decision theory with optimal-stopping principles to formalize when to act, when to wait, and how to update beliefs as evidence accumulates. The core contribution is an integrated research design that treats prediction, explanation, and governance as joint outputs of a single lifecycle: prior elicitation, likelihood construction, sequential inference, stopping rules with explicit loss functions, and post-decision auditing for robustness and accountability. Across five chapters, the book maps uncertainty into measurable objects—posterior predictive distributions, value-of-information criteria, and stopping boundaries—and then translates these objects into implementable algorithms and reproducible engineering practices. Emphasis is placed on trustworthy forecasting under distribution shift, calibration under partial observability, and policy-relevant communication of risk. Rather than relying on named datasets or specific empirical studies, the text provides portable protocols, evaluation logic, and governance artifacts that can be applied in finance, health, climate, infrastructure, and security contexts across South Asia, Europe, Africa, and the Americas. Keyword

